[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3438154621","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111959#issuecomment-3438154621","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111959","id":3438154621,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7M7hN9","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-23T17:09:13Z","updated_at":"2025-10-23T17:09:13Z","body":"Setting font size will fully recreate mesh, and for huge size like `500` it will generate huge mesh with a lot of unnecessary details, normally font size is clamped to `127`, but it's likely only enforced when using inspector. There's not much reason to use sizes above 32-48, if you need it to be bigger adjust `pixel_size` or `scale` (for dynamic resizing).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3438154621/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3438286124","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111959#issuecomment-3438286124","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111959","id":3438286124,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7M8BUs","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-23T17:38:14Z","updated_at":"2025-10-23T17:38:14Z","body":"To change the text scale at runtime efficiently, change the node's scale instead of changing font size in the TextMesh.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3438286124/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3440835748","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111959#issuecomment-3440835748","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111959","id":3440835748,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7NFvyk","user":{"login":"Supheria","id":77865986,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3ODY1OTg2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77865986?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria","html_url":"https://github.com/Supheria","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Supheria/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-24T03:50:58Z","updated_at":"2025-10-24T03:54:50Z","body":"> it will generate huge mesh with a lot of unnecessary details.\n\nBy the way, is there any way to control the detail level of TextMesh manually? Does bigger fontsize mean more details, and smaller mean less? \n\nActually, I don't need a lot details for text, I wonder there is a way to speed up text rendering by reducing detail level of TextMesh.\n\nThanks.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3440835748/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3453097705","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111959#issuecomment-3453097705","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111959","id":3453097705,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7N0hbp","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-27T20:06:43Z","updated_at":"2025-10-27T20:07:26Z","body":"> By the way, is there any way to control the detail level of TextMesh manually? Does bigger fontsize mean more details, and smaller mean less?\n\nYes, using the `curve_step` property. Lower values are *more* detailed but slower to generate/render.\n\n`font_size` also affects the font detail relative to `curve_step`, unlike `pixel_size` which simply scales the generated mesh.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3453097705/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]